{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to log crashes without generating or storing core dumps. The policy survived a full node restart and was functionally revalidated.","actions_performed":["Created /etc/systemd/coredump.conf.d/99-disable-core-dumps.conf with Storage=none and ProcessSizeMax=0.","Tested SIGSEGV handling using the local daemon service account (UID/GID 2).","Restarted node1 exactly once and verified its boot identity changed.","Repeated the crash test after restart and restored a clean system state with zero failed units."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Disable core dumps for local service-account processes","command_ids":["cmd-a8aca4e1eb2943a6","cmd-953b529bc54244d5","cmd-63c0b34bd9924a9a"],"summary":"Effective settings are Storage=none and ProcessSizeMax=0. A daemon-owned process crashed with unlimited RLIMIT_CORE; coredumpctl reported Storage: none and no core file was created."},{"requirement":"Retain normal crash logging","command_ids":["cmd-953b529bc54244d5","cmd-6d56e4c5953b42e7","cmd-63c0b34bd9924a9a"],"summary":"Both pre- and post-restart SIGSEGV tests produced systemd and structured journald records containing the process, UID/GID, signal, executable, and service unit."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-e6059ec280b3489f","cmd-c2531be8b89c4653","cmd-695a18065a2647ae","cmd-5a4336cac031499d","cmd-acbe06284928445e"],"summary":"Healthy baseline was captured on boot 45c22b1f-31bf-419b-a1a4-331c4aa1a40a, reboot acknowledgement returned, and node1 recovered on boot 65e886a6-0407-48e3-abd1-f132315f4088. Journald, systemd-coredump.socket, and sshd are active; the system is running with zero failed units, the policy remains effective, and stored core count is zero."}]}
